clang Frontend: read the layout-override and layout-seed files through
llvm::MemoryBuffer instead of std::ifstream

Failure: with the C kit's libc++ (filesystem library off, as for C++0),
`implicit instantiation of undefined template 'std::basic_ifstream<char>'`
at clang/lib/Frontend/CompilerInvocation.cpp:4210
(-frandomize-layout-seed-file=) and LayoutOverrideSource.cpp:43
(-foverride-record-layout=).
Change: both files are read with llvm::MemoryBuffer::getFile (text mode):
the seed is the file's first line; the layout parser iterates over the
same lines the std::getline loop produced, including the empty one after a
final newline. No #if: the change applies to every platform.
Behaviour preserved: the same diagnostic when the seed file cannot be
opened; the same lines in the same order to the layout parser; file reads
use the same path every other clang input uses (on ABSD: into the heap).
Upstreamability: high; clang elsewhere reads files through the
FileManager/MemoryBuffer and avoids iostreams (LLVM coding standards:
"#include <iostream> is forbidden").

